\p{Current proposed scope is specified by the active decisions that name this test.}
\p{Named by: \ref{dec-kr-0015}.}
\p{\em{Lean declaration(s):} the general theorem remains unstated; partial comparison lemmas are indexed below.}

\p{\strong{Partial implementation evidence:} \ref{augmented-generating} records the checked monad algebra-lifting and essential-image lemma and its transfer through supplied monadic comparisons. The general arity-to-exactness argument is not yet proved; this does not pass or weaken the gate.}

\p{\strong{Monad-algebra reconstruction evidence:} \ref{augmented-monad-vertical} reconstructs vertical categories and functors from arbitrary generating-monad algebras, retains the horizontal graph and proves a natural equivalence recovering each existing augmented algebra's vertical category. \ref{augmented-monad-cells} adds incident cells, all primitive operations and a surjective full-boundary evaluation map preserving both identities and arbitrary substitution. \ref{augmented-monadicity} now proves all five reconstructed equation families, identifies the action and proves essential surjectivity and monadicity. \ref{augmented-arity-nerve} constructs the actual nerve square and its canonical comparison, proving conditional recognition under density and comparison invertibility. \ref{augmented-finite-incidence} supplies a small dense candidate family; its monad exactness and the labelled diagram model remain open.}

\p{\strong{Finite incidence candidate:} \ref{augmented-finite-incidence} proves closure of finite generators under complete incidence, filtered reconstruction of each generating presheaf, and the equivalence between finite incidence and finite presentability. It constructs a small fully faithful dense candidate family of finite incidence diagrams and applies the conditional nerve theorem. Canonical-comparison invertibility for the generating monad remains open; no normalization or labelled diagram-model result is asserted. The full acceptance statements and statuses remain unchanged.}
